Now the JS. Need to be meticulous. Let me outline code.

Constants, state.

I'll write in an IIFE.

DOM:
const canvas... ctx.
const ui = { score, speed, hudBest, ... overlay, screens, startBtn... }

State object:
const G = {
 state:'menu',
 t:0,
 scroll:0,
 speed:360,
 score:0,
 best: load,
 lane:1,
 player:{x:0,y:0,prevX:0,lean:0,w:0,h:0},
 vehicles:[],
 particles:[],
 floats:[],
 streaks:[],
 spawnTimer:0,
 crashTimer:0,
 crashVehicle:null,
 shake:0,
 demoLaneTimer:0,
 toast:null,
 laneW:0, roadX:0, roadW:0, W:0,H:0,
 level:1,
 nearMissCount...
};

Better separate layout fields.

Seeded rng for scenery.

Sounds.

Canvas resize.

Road pattern: create canvas 160; dots. Grass maybe base.

Scenery creation.

Input setup.

Functions: resetGame(start), gameOver(v), showScreen(name), updateHUD.

Loop.

Let me code with careful ordering (functions hoisted mostly function declarations).

Key details:

Resize:
function resize() {
  W = window.innerWidth; H = window.innerHeight;
  DPR = Math.min(2, window.devicePixelRatio || 1);
  canvas.width = Math.round(W*DPR); canvas.height=Math.round(H*DPR);
  canvas.style.width = W+'px'; canvas.style.height=H+'px';
  ctx.setTransform(DPR,0,0,DPR,0,0);
  computeLayout();
  buildScenery();
  if (G.player.x) { G.player.x = laneX(G.lane); } else nothing.
}
Careful: set player's y and target. On resize during play, clamp x.

computeLayout:
const gap = Math.max(16, Math.min(96, W*0.075));
roadW = Math.max(240, Math.min(W - gap*2, 720)); // if W < 272 weird; phones >=320 → W-2*24=272 >240.
But max with 240 might exceed W for W=320? 320-48=272 fine. For W=280 gap 21 → 238 → max 240 > W? W-42=238. Road 240 with 20px sides. Fine. Not important.
roadX=(W-roadW)/2;
laneW=roadW/4;
playerY = Math.min(H-110, Math.max(H*0.72, H-250)); Hmm choose simple: H*0.78; clamp between H*0.62 and H-96.
playerY = Math.min(H - 92, Math.max(H*0.62, H*0.78));
For H=800 => 624; H=400 => 311 (H*0.78=312, min 308) -> 308. Good.
bike.w = Math.max(20, laneW*0.36); bike.h = Math.max(46, laneW*0.92);
player.y = playerY.
Touch controls at bottom 18+76 = 94, bike center at 624 bottom around 683 (bike h=149 half 74) for H800; buttons bottom ~724 top ~648, they might overlap bike horizontally? Buttons at far edges; bike center; fine.

Scenery:
const SC_PERIOD = 2200;
buildScenery uses laneW and roadX:
function buildScenery(){
  const rs = mulberry?
  let s = 987654321;
  const rnd = () => { s = (s*1664525 + 1013904223) >>> 0; return s/4294967296; };
  scenery = [];
  for (const side of [-1,1]) {
    let y = rnd()*220;
    while (y < SC_PERIOD) {
      const pick = rnd();
      let type;
      if (pick < .30) type='tree';
      else if (pick<.44) type='palm';
      else if (pick<.54) type='bush';
      else if (pick<.63) type='pole';
      else if (pick<.72) type='grass';
      else if (pick<.80) type='paddy';
      else if (pick<.90) type='hut';
      else type='pond';
      const sizeBase = laneW;
      let size = ...
      item = { side, y, type, depth: 0.1+rnd()*.75, v: rnd(), size };
      // skip if can't fit
      if ((type==='hut'||type==='pond'||type==='paddy') && roadX < 74) skip -> maybe fallback to grass/bush
      push.
      y += size*? + 30 + rnd()*120;
    }
  }
}
Define sizes:
tree: 0.16..0.28 * laneW radius? laneW 84 → 13-23 px radius; small but okay. On desktop lane 180 → 29-50. Good.
palm: 0.18-0.28.
bush: 0.09-0.15.
pole: 0.12 (use size as width).
grass: 0.06.
paddy: width = min(roadX*1.1, laneW*1.6), height = laneW*.8; size = width (will treat w) plus h.
hut: w = min(roadX*0.72, laneW*0.9); h = w*0.66. require roadX > w*0.8.
pond: w = min(roadX*1.25, laneW*2.2); h = w*0.55.
Need item.w/h computed per type. Store w,h.

Simplify: item.w and item.h computed:
tree/palm/bush: w=h=size*2 (diameter).
pole: w=size*1.5,h=size*3? Draw small.
grass: w=size*2,h=size*1.5.
paddy: w=...,h=...
hut/pond similarly.

Depth used to place.

Regenerate on resize; scenery uses laneW, roadX. Need deterministic; reset seed each call.

Drawing scenery item:
function sceneryPos(item, yOff) {
 const pad = 7;
 let cx;
 const free = Math.max(0, roadX - pad*2);
 if item.side<0:
   const near = roadX - pad - item.w/2;
   const far = pad + item.w/2;
   cx = near + (far-near)*item.depth; // depth 0 near, 1 far; but if far>near for narrow? ensure
 else mirrored.
 But for wide sides, depth .1 is near road (good).
 For pond/hut depth choose .3-.8.
If item.w > free, cx maybe clipped; skip if item.w > roadX - 4? For hut pond, computed to fit.
y position: wrap.
}

Actually for narrow mobile side ~22px width, even tree w 40 won't fit; tree will overlap road. Need skip items whose w > roadX*1.6? Draw partially cut at edge is okay if centered within side with clipping? Road drawn after scenery, so trees overlapping onto road get covered by road! Since road drawn after scenery. Great: scenery can extend under road and be hidden. But trees may overlap road edge strangely? Road covers. So no issue. But objects might be drawn under road partly, fine. Draw scenery before road. But huts may be hidden; acceptable.

However poles/flags should be at edge visible; draw after road? If scenery drawn before road, flags near edge still visible outside road. Fine.

Draw background: grass gradient, alternating field bands, then scenery, then road.

We need HUD z-level separate.

Update functions:

function resetGame(){
  G.score=0; G.speed=340; G.scroll=0; G.vehicles=[]; G.particles=[]; G.floats=[]; G.streaks=[];
  G.spawnTimer=.45; G.crashTimer=0; G.crashVehicle=null; G.shake=0; G.lane=1; G.player.x=laneX(1); G.player.prevX=G.player.x; G.player.lean=0;
  G.level=1; G.toast=null; G.elapsed=0; G.nearMisses=0;
  crash.angle=0; crash.spin=0; crash.active=false;
  ui.score.textContent='0'; updateHUD(true);
}

Start:
function startGame(){
  Sound.init(); Sound.startEngine();
  resetGame();
  setState('playing');
  hideOverlay();
  G.runStartedAt = performance.now();
}
setState(s){ G.state=s; document.body.dataset.state=s; update buttons/screens? }
showOverlay(screenId): overlay.classList.remove('hidden'); hide all screens except screenId.

Need state transitions:
menu → start → playing.
playing → pause → paused.
paused→resume.
playing→crash→over.
over→restart→playing.
Menu overlay shown initially (overlay visible, menu screen).
Overlay DOM: `#overlay` visible by default. `#menuScreen` visible. Others hidden.
hideOverlay: overlay.classList.add('hidden'); after transition maybe keep pointer none. `.overlay.hidden` has pointer-events none so fine.
showOverlay(id): overlay.classList.remove('hidden'); screens each toggle hidden. state set accordingly.

Pause function:
if playing → setState('paused'); showOverlay('pauseScreen'); Sound.pauseEngine().
resume → hide overlay, state playing, Sound.resumeEngine().

On crash: G.state='crash'; crashTimer=0; crash.active=true; shake=18; Sound.crash(); spawn particles; store crashVehicle name; body state 'crash'? CSS no specific. Keep hud. After 0.9s in update → finishGame(): setState('over'); show overlay with stats; save best; Sound.stopEngine().

G.state 'over' continue update slow.

Update(dt):
G.t += dt; (animation time); but paused no update so t frozen — fine.

if state menu:
  G.demoTimer -= dt; if <=0 set demo target lane random; 
  demo move x toward laneX(demoLane);
  scroll += 250*dt;
  speed display? Set G.speed=250;
  spawn vehicles with G.spawnTimer using roadSpeed 250 no score; update vehicles; collisions ignored; remove.
