spawnVehicle can take yOffset. Simpler after spawn: v.y -= stagger. Different lengths. Fine.

Difficulty: state.level increments based score; maybe speed clamp 980.

Vehicles update:
```
function updateVehicles(dt, slow=false){
 for (let i=vehicles.length-1;i>=0;i--){
  const v=vehicles[i];
  const rel = state.speed + v.onSpeed*(slow?0.15:1);
  v.y += rel*dt;
  v.sway += dt*1.5;
  if(!v.passed && v.y - v.l*0.5 > playerY + bike.h*0.5){
    v.passed=true;
    if(state.mode==='playing'){
      const dx=Math.abs(v.x-player.x);
      if(dx<laneW*1.02){const pts=dx<laneW*.7?30:15; state.score+=pts; addFloat('+'+pts+(pts>20?'  CLOSE!':'  NEAR MISS'), player.x, playerY-50, '#ffcf4a', .85, Math.max(11,laneW*.08));}
    }
  }
  if(v.y - v.l*0.5 > H+120) vehicles.splice(i,1);
 }
}
```
Note near-miss bonus when the vehicle passes player: condition vehicle top passes player bottom. Fine.

Check collision after updates. Also add gentle horn occasionally when vehicle near top? Horn timer in playing: every 6-10 sec call Sound.horn() if soundOn. Add in update.

Player lane movement:
```
